@startuml ClassDiagram
allowmixing
title Week 2 — original Todo App (starter b32ff42)
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

class TodoManager {
  + tasks: Array<Object>
  + container: HTMLElement
  + TodoManager(containerId)
  + loadTasks()
  + saveTasks()
  + addTask(description, type): boolean
  + toggleComplete(id)
  + deleteTask(id)
  + renderPendingRows(): String
  + renderCompletedRows(): String
  + render(justAddedId)
}

rectangle "localStorage\ngetItem(key) / setItem(key, value)" as Storage <<browser API>>
rectangle "DOM / document\ncontainer, buttons, title" as DOM <<browser API>>
rectangle "buildTaskRow(id, desc, completed,\npriority, createdAt, showActions)" as RowHelper <<free function>>
rectangle "Workload summary helper\nreads manager.tasks" as SummaryHelper <<free function>>
rectangle "DOMContentLoaded listener\nconstructs manager and binds Add / Enter" as Startup <<startup function>>

TodoManager ..> Storage : directly reads / writes
TodoManager --> DOM : keeps a container reference
TodoManager ..> RowHelper : builds pending / completed rows
TodoManager ..> SummaryHelper : requests status text
SummaryHelper ..> TodoManager : inspects public tasks
Startup ..> TodoManager : creates and calls
Startup ..> DOM : binds input events

note left of TodoManager
  The only declared class in src/todo.js.
  All its properties and methods are public.
  It owns the tasks array and creates plain records:
  id, desc, completed, priority, createdAt.
  There is no Task, TodoList, or Storage class.
end note

note bottom of Storage
  Browser API dependency, not an owned part.
  Saved records survive destruction of the manager.
end note

note bottom of DOM
  Reference to an existing element, not composition.
  The page owns its lifetime; the manager updates it.
end note
@enduml
